<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had planted 28.8 percent of their planned total 6.8 million hectare wheat area by October 4, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Wheat in Buenos Aires, outside the province's northwest, and in La Pampa, outside the north was in good shape. The crop in those areas was helped by recent rain which allowed the completion of fertilization and weed-control work. But wheat in parts of northwestern Buenos Aires, Cordoba, Entre Rios and northern La Pampa were hit by lack of rain and their yields will suffer.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
